Return JSON only (no markdown). Schema enforces exactly num_beats beats and named primitive params.
Rules still apply: musically coherent choices, immediate PLAN tails for multi-beat primitives, transition PLAN between different primitives, at most 4 multi-beat primitives, respect bounds and step limits.
Each choreography action must be an object: {"primitive":"name","params":{...}}.
Use exactly the parameter names from the primitive signature. PLAN uses empty params: {"primitive":"PLAN","params":{}}.

Correct JSON param examples:
- center([ids]) -> {"primitive":"center","params":{"drone_ids":[1,2,3,4]}}
- move_z([ids], delta_cm) -> {"primitive":"move_z","params":{"drone_ids":[1,2,3,4],"delta_cm":30}}
- form_cone(delta_height_cm, spacing_cm, is_inverted) -> {"primitive":"form_cone","params":{"delta_height_cm":60,"spacing_cm":60,"is_inverted":0}}
- spiral_speed(steps, height_cm, degrees, radius_increase) -> {"primitive":"spiral_speed","params":{"steps":3,"height_cm":100,"degrees":180,"radius_increase":1}}
- wave(steps, height_cm, mu_pairs, a_mu, b_mu) -> {"primitive":"wave","params":{"steps":2,"height_cm":80,"mu_pairs":[[0,0],[1,0]],"a_mu":[0.5,0.25],"b_mu":[0.2,0.1]}}

Common mistakes that will fail syntax checks:
- Wrong: {"primitive":"form_cone","params":{"drone_ids":[1,2,3],"delta_height_cm":60,"spacing_cm":60,"is_inverted":0}} because form_cone has no drone_ids param.
- Wrong: {"primitive":"spiral_speed","params":{"steps":3,"height_cm":100,"angle_deg":90,"degrees":180,"radius_increase":1}} because spiral_speed has no angle_deg param.
- Wrong: {"primitive":"move_z","params":{"delta_cm":30}} because move_z also needs drone_ids.

